+## Turn usage (issue #93)
+
+The chosen contract retains one usage argument and sums each token field across provider calls. A per-round breakdown is rejected for this change because billing and budgets need the turn total and retaining the argument shape minimizes consumer migration. The public hook signature must name its usage type or argument as a turn total; the implementation must include a MINOR version bump and a changelog entry explaining that existing consumers record larger totals for turns using tools.
+
+- `afterModelResponse` fires once per user message after the round loop exits and receives the sum of `inputTokens`, `outputTokens`, and `totalTokens` across every provider call, including both tool rounds and the final response ([validated by: reports the sum of all three provider calls after two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L71)).
+- Missing usage contributes nothing to the sum, whether before, between, or after reported rounds; a turn where no provider call reports usage receives `undefined`, including after a previous turn reported usage ([validated by: sums reported rounds around missing usage and leaves wholly unreported turns undefined](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L80)).
+- A turn without tools retains its existing response text and usage values ([validated by: receives collected response text and usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.test.ts#L236)).
+
 ## Measured semantics — out of scope
 
-These two properties of `src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts` are recorded so the hook features that follow specify against real behaviour. This issue changes none of them; each is a separate, out-of-scope change owned by no issue in this epic.
+The following existing behaviour is independent of usage accounting and remains outside issue #93.
 
-- The `catch` gates `onError` on `error instanceof Error` ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L150](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L150)), so a rejection that is not an `Error` — a thrown string or object — bypasses `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller.
-- `afterModelResponse` is called once per user message after the round loop exits ([chatOrchestrator.ts#L148](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.ts#L148)), and is passed the `lastUsage` local — the most recent round's usage, not a sum across tool rounds, so a deployer using the hook for billing or audit under-counts every turn that ran tools.
